    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56af-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AF(2) Information Commissioner must analyse and report about an",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56af-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, before making a recommendation under subsection (1),\nthe Commission must do all of the following:\n\n(a) analyse the matters in paragraphs 56AD(1)(a) to (d) in\nrelation to the proposed instrument;\n\n(b) consult the public about those matters in relation to the\nproposed instrument:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that includes making information\navailable on the Commission’s website and inviting the\npublic to comment;\n\n(c) consult each of the persons or bodies covered by\nparagraph 56AE(1)(c) about those matters in relation to the\nproposed instrument;\n\n(d) report to the Minister about that analysis and consultation;\n\n(e) publish the report on the Commission’s website.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, before making a recommendation under subsection (1),\nthe Commission must do all of the following:\n\n(a) analyse the matters in paragraphs 56AD(1)(a) to (d) in\nrelation to the proposed instrument;\n\n(b) consult the public about those matters in relation to the\nproposed instrument:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that includes making information\navailable on the Commission’s website and inviting the\npublic to comment;\n\n(c) consult each of the persons or bodies covered by\nparagraph 56AE(1)(c) about those matters in relation to the\nproposed instrument;\n\n(d) report to the Minister about that analysis and consultation;\n\n(e) publish the report on the Commission’s website.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56af"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56af-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56af-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56af-ss-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "311b0c137d0ed10030a28f645614215d6c8acf3990fc985066ef72a6ae348ead",
      "skos:note": "Information Commissioner must publish report on website, except for excluded part. The Information Commissioner must analyse and report about the proposed instrument.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56af-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AF(2) Information Commissioner must analyse and report about an",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, before making a recommendation under subsection (1),\nthe Commission must do all of the following:\n\n(a) analyse the matters in paragraphs 56AD(1)(a) to (d) in\nrelation to the proposed instrument;\n\n(b) consult the public about those matters in relation to the\nproposed instrument:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that includes making information\navailable on the Commission’s website and inviting the\npublic to comment;\n\n(c) consult each of the persons or bodies covered by\nparagraph 56AE(1)(c) about those matters in relation to the\nproposed instrument;\n\n(d) report to the Minister about that analysis and consultation;\n\n(e) publish the report on the Commission’s website."
    },
