    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ao-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AO(5) Extraterritorial operation of the CDR provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ao-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nAustralia, when used in a geographical sense, includes all the\nexternal Territories.\nAustralian person means:\n\n(a) a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; or\n\n(b) an Australian citizen, a permanent resident (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007), or any other\nperson ordinarily resident within Australia or an external\nTerritory; or\n\n(c) an entity covered by subsection 56AR(1), (2) or (3) (about\nAustralian government entities).\nforeign person means a person other than an Australian person.\npoint includes a mobile or potentially mobile point, whether on\nland, underground, in the atmosphere, underwater, at sea or\nanywhere else.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In this section:\nAustralia, when used in a geographical sense, includes all the\nexternal Territories.\nAustralian person means:\n\n(a) a body corporate established by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; or\n\n(b) an Australian citizen, a permanent resident (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007), or any other\nperson ordinarily resident within Australia or an external\nTerritory; or\n\n(c) an entity covered by subsection 56AR(1), (2) or (3) (about\nAustralian government entities).\nforeign person means a person other than an Australian person.\npoint includes a mobile or potentially mobile point, whether on\nland, underground, in the atmosphere, underwater, at sea or\nanywhere else.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ao"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ao-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
