      "cml:premiseText": "(2) The CDR provisions apply only in relation to an entity that..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ar-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AR(3) Government entities may participate under this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ar-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, whether or not such a declaration is in force for an entity\nreferred to in subsection (2), the CDR provisions apply in relation\nto the entity to the extent that:\n\n(a) the CDR provisions relate to a CDR consumer for CDR data;\nand\n\n(b) the entity is a CDR consumer for CDR data (or would be a\nCDR consumer for CDR data if the entity were a person).\nNote:\nFor how the CDR provisions so apply, see subsection (4).\nHow the CDR provisions apply to a government entity",
      "skos:definition": "(3) However, whether or not such a declaration is in force for an entity\nreferred to in subsection (2), the CDR provisions apply in relation\nto the entity to the extent that:\n\n(a) the CDR provisions relate to a CDR consumer for CDR data;\nand\n\n(b) the entity is a CDR consumer for CDR data (or would be a\nCDR consumer for CDR data if the entity were a person).\nNote:\nFor how the CDR provisions so apply, see subsection (4).\nHow the CDR provisions apply to a government entity",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ar"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ar-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ar-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d8efd7d5ec44799e4875ff610a138e3c0cac278ed8476d74884934a8feb5080a",
      "skos:note": "Government entities must comply with CDR provisions for CDR data they are consumers of."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ar-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AR(3) Government entities may participate under this Part",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, whether or not such a declaration is in force for an entity\nreferred to in subsection (2), the CDR provisions apply in relation\nto the entity to the extent that:\n\n(a) the CDR provisions relate to a CDR consumer for CDR data;\nand\n\n(b) the entity is a CDR consumer for CDR data (or would be a\nCDR consumer for CDR data if the entity were a person).\nNote:\nFor how the CDR provisions so apply, see subsection (4).\nHow the CDR provisions apply to a government entity"
    },
    {
