    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56as",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AS Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56as"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "declaration\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, declare that an entity is\na participating entity for a State or Territory.\nNote:\nAn entity may be specified by class (see subsection 13(3) of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\n\n(2) However, the Minister must not do so unless the Minister is\nsatisfied that the State or Territory has agreed to the entity\nparticipating under this Part.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a State or Territory has agreed to an entity of the State or\nTerritory participating under this Part; and\n\n(b) the entity is a body corporate;\nthe entity is taken to have also agreed to participate under this Part.",
      "skos:definition": "declaration\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, declare that an entity is\na participating entity for a State or Territory.\nNote:\nAn entity may be specified by class (see subsection 13(3) of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\n\n(2) However, the Minister must not do so unless the Minister is\nsatisfied that the State or Territory has agreed to the entity\nparticipating under this Part.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a State or Territory has agreed to an entity of the State or\nTerritory participating under this Part; and\n\n(b) the entity is a body corporate;\nthe entity is taken to have also agreed to participate under this Part.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56as-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56as-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56as-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "abcd0ee1fc2cdf511d8a85bd020c5f2f18468d6c442f5506fec7d859b8fea335"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56as",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AS Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "declaration\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, declare that an entity is\na participating entity for a State or Territory.\nNote:\nAn entity may be specified by class (see subsection 13(3) of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\n\n(2) However, the Minister must not do so unless the Minister is\nsatisfied that the State or Territory has agreed to the entity\nparticipating under this Part.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a State or Territory has agreed to an entity of the State or\nTerritory participating under this Part; and\n\n(b) the entity is a body corporate;\nthe entity is taken to have also agreed to participate under this Part."
    },
