    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56at",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56AT Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56at"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "revocation\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, revoke a declaration\nmade under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a participating\nentity for a State or Territory.\n\n(2) If a State or Territory requests in writing the Minister to revoke a\ndeclaration made under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a\nparticipating entity for the State or Territory, the Minister must,\nunder subsection (1) of this section, revoke the declaration as soon\nas practicable.\n\n(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019",
      "skos:definition": "revocation\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, revoke a declaration\nmade under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a participating\nentity for a State or Territory.\n\n(2) If a State or Territory requests in writing the Minister to revoke a\ndeclaration made under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a\nparticipating entity for the State or Territory, the Minister must,\nunder subsection (1) of this section, revoke the declaration as soon\nas practicable.\n\n(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56at-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56at-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56at-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a3c5fe92785106889f22a9633aef8bd8ff1ca1d6a82f3808ecc732dc56b12bd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56at",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AT Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "revocation\n\n(1) The Minister may, by notifiable instrument, revoke a declaration\nmade under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a participating\nentity for a State or Territory.\n\n(2) If a State or Territory requests in writing the Minister to revoke a\ndeclaration made under subsection 56AS(1) that an entity is a\nparticipating entity for the State or Territory, the Minister must,\nunder subsection (1) of this section, revoke the declaration as soon\nas practicable.\n\n(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019"
    },
