          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56at-ss-3-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90875b77d2361d9c979a9fb63f96fce8ab723e12febfa7f59877a94e8e0fb342",
      "skos:note": "Continues to apply certain rights, privileges, obligations or liabilities after revocation of declaration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56at-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56AT(3) Participating government entities of a State or Territory—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the Minister revokes a declaration made under\nsubsection 56AS(1) in relation to an entity, then, despite the\nrevocation, subsection 56AR(2) continues to apply to the entity in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued\nor incurred before the revocation; and\n\n(b) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of\nany such right, privilege, obligation or liability;\nas if the declaration were still in force.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019"
    },
