    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ba",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BA Commission may make consumer data rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ba"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, make rules (the\nconsumer data rules) for designated sectors in accordance with\nthis Division.\nNote:\nSubdivision C deals with the process for making the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the consumer data rules may set\nout:\n\n(a) different rules for different designated sectors; or\n\n(b) different rules for different classes of CDR data; or\n\n(c) different rules for different classes of persons specified, as\ndescribed in paragraph 56AC(2)(b), in an instrument\ndesignating a sector under subsection 56AC(2); or\n\n(d) different rules for different classes of persons who are able to\nbe disclosed CDR data under the consumer data rules.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, make rules (the\nconsumer data rules) for designated sectors in accordance with\nthis Division.\nNote:\nSubdivision C deals with the process for making the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the consumer data rules may set\nout:\n\n(a) different rules for different designated sectors; or\n\n(b) different rules for different classes of CDR data; or\n\n(c) different rules for different classes of persons specified, as\ndescribed in paragraph 56AC(2)(b), in an instrument\ndesignating a sector under subsection 56AC(2); or\n\n(d) different rules for different classes of persons who are able to\nbe disclosed CDR data under the consumer data rules.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ba-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ba-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7163d980366f3264d5de96ebfa2900ef2e2895dd363864ed891d9b5eb4f9db53"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ba",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BA Commission may make consumer data rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by legislative instrument, make rules (the\nconsumer data rules) for designated sectors in accordance with\nthis Division.\nNote:\nSubdivision C deals with the process for making the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the consumer data rules may set\nout:\n\n(a) different rules for different designated sectors; or\n\n(b) different rules for different classes of CDR data; or\n\n(c) different rules for different classes of persons specified, as\ndescribed in paragraph 56AC(2)(b), in an instrument\ndesignating a sector under subsection 56AC(2); or\n\n(d) different rules for different classes of persons who are able to\nbe disclosed CDR data under the consumer data rules."
    },
