      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bd-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires disclosure of designated CDR data for which there are one or more CDR consumers.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bd-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "within",
      "cml:logicSummary": "CDR data must be within a class of information specified in an instrument designating a sector.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56be",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BE Rules about disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56be"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "security or deletion of product data\n\nWithout limiting paragraph 56BB(b), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules for CDR data for which there are no\nCDR consumers:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for the CDR data to\ndisclose all or part of the CDR data to a person in response to\na valid request by the person;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a person may make a valid request of the kind\ndescribed in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person to satisfy in order to be disclosed\nthe CDR data in the way described in paragraph (a);\n\n(d) other rules affecting:\n\n(i) CDR participants for the CDR data; or\n\n(ii) persons wishing to be disclosed the CDR data;\n\nthat relate to the disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,\nsecurity or deletion of the CDR data.\nNote 1:\nA request for this CDR data could be made, for example, to assist the\ndevelopment of a product or service.\nNote 2:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 3:\nThe privacy safeguards do not apply to this CDR data (see\nsubsection 56EB(1)).",
      "skos:definition": "security or deletion of product data\n\nWithout limiting paragraph 56BB(b), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules for CDR data for which there are no\nCDR consumers:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for the CDR data to\ndisclose all or part of the CDR data to a person in response to\na valid request by the person;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a person may make a valid request of the kind\ndescribed in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person to satisfy in order to be disclosed\nthe CDR data in the way described in paragraph (a);\n\n(d) other rules affecting:\n\n(i) CDR participants for the CDR data; or\n\n(ii) persons wishing to be disclosed the CDR data;\n\nthat relate to the disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,\nsecurity or deletion of the CDR data.\nNote 1:\nA request for this CDR data could be made, for example, to assist the\ndevelopment of a product or service.\nNote 2:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 3:\nThe privacy safeguards do not apply to this CDR data (see\nsubsection 56EB(1)).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56be-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56be-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d31ba371915e189affb588ba5aad4a78211a51888bbabdd01c703aae233f90bf",
      "skos:note": "Rules for disclosure of CDR data to a person in response to a valid request."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56be",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BE Rules about disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "security or deletion of product data\n\nWithout limiting paragraph 56BB(b), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules for CDR data for which there are no\nCDR consumers:\n\n(a) requirements on a CDR participant for the CDR data to\ndisclose all or part of the CDR data to a person in response to\na valid request by the person;\n\n(b) rules about:\n\n(i) how a person may make a valid request of the kind\ndescribed in paragraph (a); and\n\n(ii) what must be included in a request for it to be valid,\nwhat disclosures or other matters a valid request may\ncover, and when a request ceases to be a valid request;\n\n(c) requirements on a person to satisfy in order to be disclosed\nthe CDR data in the way described in paragraph (a);\n\n(d) other rules affecting:\n\n(i) CDR participants for the CDR data; or\n\n(ii) persons wishing to be disclosed the CDR data;\n\nthat relate to the disclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage,\nsecurity or deletion of the CDR data.\nNote 1:\nA request for this CDR data could be made, for example, to assist the\ndevelopment of a product or service.\nNote 2:\nThe requirements described in paragraph (a) could, for example,\ninclude a requirement that the disclosure be in accordance with the\nrelevant data standards.\nNote 3:\nThe privacy safeguards do not apply to this CDR data (see\nsubsection 56EB(1))."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56be-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56be"
