        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56be-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must disclose CDR data",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Valid request",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Disclosure of CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BF Limitations for rules about product data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are no CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is about the eligibility criteria, terms and\nconditions, price, availability or performance of:\n\n(i) a product or other kind of good; or\n\n(ii) a service; and\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are no CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is about the eligibility criteria, terms and\nconditions, price, availability or performance of:\n\n(i) a product or other kind of good; or\n\n(ii) a service; and\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bf-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bf-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e6b58766753c0aaf367680cd595819058187810d15566d538796b5aed1d9cf12",
      "skos:note": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BF Limitations for rules about product data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "Only certain kinds of product data can be required to be disclosed\n\n(1) The consumer data rules can only require a disclosure of CDR data\nfor which there are no CDR consumers if:\n\n(a) the CDR data is about the eligibility criteria, terms and\nconditions, price, availability or performance of:\n\n(i) a product or other kind of good; or\n\n(ii) a service; and\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bf"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bf-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the obligation to disclose certain kinds of product data",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The text imposes an obligation to disclose certain kinds of product data",
      "cml:conclusionText": "There is an obligation to disclose certain kinds of product data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BG Rules about designated gateways",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "CDR data for which there are CDR consumers\n\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(c), if there is a designated\ngateway for CDR data for which there are one or more CDR\nconsumers, the consumer data rules may include the following\nrules:\n\n(a) rules like those described in subsection 56BC(1) for the CDR\ndata, but involving the designated gateway:\n\n(i) acting between the CDR consumer and the CDR\nparticipant in the making of a valid request; or\n\n(ii) acting between the CDR consumer and the accredited\nperson who is the proposed recipient of the requested\ndisclosure; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(iii) acting between the CDR participant and the CDR\nconsumer, or accredited person, who is the proposed\nrecipient of the requested disclosure;\n\n(b) rules like those described in subsection 56BC(2) for the CDR\ndata, but involving the designated gateway:\n\n(i) acting between the CDR consumer and a person\nauthorised as described in that subsection; or\n\n(ii) acting between persons authorised as described in that\nsubsection;\n\n(c) other rules affecting the designated gateway that relate to the\ndisclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of the CDR data.\nProduct data\n\n(2) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(c), if there is a designated\ngateway for CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers, the\nconsumer data rules may include the following rules:\n\n(a) rules like those described in paragraphs 56BE(a) to (c), but\ninvolving the designated gateway acting between the CDR\nparticipant and the person requesting the disclosure;\n\n(b) other rules affecting the designated gateway that relate to the\ndisclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of the CDR data.\nLimitation—rules relating to the collection, use, accuracy, storage,\nsecurity or deletion of CDR data\n\n(3) For a designated gateway for CDR data for which there are one or\nmore CDR consumers, the consumer data rules:\n\n(a) can only include rules affecting the designated gateway\nrequiring or authorising the disclosure of the CDR data if\nsuch rules are as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b); and\n\n(b) can only include rules affecting the designated gateway that\nrelate to the collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of the CDR data if such rules also relate to a\ndisclosure described in paragraph (a) of this subsection.\nNote:\nParagraph (a) does not prevent the inclusion of a rule relating to a\ndisclosure described in that paragraph.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite any other provision of this Division.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "CDR data for which there are CDR consumers\n\n(1) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(c), if there is a designated\ngateway for CDR data for which there are one or more CDR\nconsumers, the consumer data rules may include the following\nrules:\n\n(a) rules like those described in subsection 56BC(1) for the CDR\ndata, but involving the designated gateway:\n\n(i) acting between the CDR consumer and the CDR\nparticipant in the making of a valid request; or\n\n(ii) acting between the CDR consumer and the accredited\nperson who is the proposed recipient of the requested\ndisclosure; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(iii) acting between the CDR participant and the CDR\nconsumer, or accredited person, who is the proposed\nrecipient of the requested disclosure;\n\n(b) rules like those described in subsection 56BC(2) for the CDR\ndata, but involving the designated gateway:\n\n(i) acting between the CDR consumer and a person\nauthorised as described in that subsection; or\n\n(ii) acting between persons authorised as described in that\nsubsection;\n\n(c) other rules affecting the designated gateway that relate to the\ndisclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of the CDR data.\nProduct data\n\n(2) Without limiting paragraph 56BB(c), if there is a designated\ngateway for CDR data for which there are no CDR consumers, the\nconsumer data rules may include the following rules:\n\n(a) rules like those described in paragraphs 56BE(a) to (c), but\ninvolving the designated gateway acting between the CDR\nparticipant and the person requesting the disclosure;\n\n(b) other rules affecting the designated gateway that relate to the\ndisclosure, collection, use, accuracy, storage, security or\ndeletion of the CDR data.\nLimitation—rules relating to the collection, use, accuracy, storage,\nsecurity or deletion of CDR data\n\n(3) For a designated gateway for CDR data for which there are one or\nmore CDR consumers, the cons",
