      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), each of the following may be a\nground for varying, suspending or revoking an accreditation:\n\n(a) a failure to comply with a requirement in this Part or in the\nconsumer data rules;\n\n(b) a failure to comply with a requirement in the privacy\nsafeguards.\nNote:\nAn example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or\nchanging the level of an accreditation.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), each of the following may be a\nground for varying, suspending or revoking an accreditation:\n\n(a) a failure to comply with a requirement in this Part or in the\nconsumer data rules;\n\n(b) a failure to comply with a requirement in the privacy\nsafeguards.\nNote:\nAn example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or\nchanging the level of an accreditation.",
      "values:partOf": {
