      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df6ca88c124ad3ecd57cf6364cd86b4f63b5d95f34228cf39795fc66d1f28512",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with requirements may result in varying, suspending or revoking accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BH(3) Rules about accreditation of data recipients",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), each of the following may be a\nground for varying, suspending or revoking an accreditation:\n\n(a) a failure to comply with a requirement in this Part or in the\nconsumer data rules;\n\n(b) a failure to comply with a requirement in the privacy\nsafeguards.\nNote:\nAn example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or\nchanging the level of an accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
