        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f7e664093a361179ce18b8ef1567ed2175527515eff35a81127ddde84ee5a7d",
      "skos:note": "Must permit applications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of decisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BH(4) Rules about accreditation of data recipients",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the consumer data rules include rules enabling decisions to be\nmade to vary, suspend or revoke accreditations, the rules must\npermit the making of applications to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of those decisions.\nNote:\nThe consumer data rules can also provide for internal review of these\ndecisions, and internal and AAT review of other decisions (see\nsection 56BJ)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-4-norm",
