    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BJ Rules about incidental or related matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "Without limiting paragraph 56BB(f), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) rules that refer to the data standards;\n\n(b) the circumstances in which persons are, or may be, relieved\nfrom complying with requirements in the consumer data rules\nthat would otherwise apply to them;\n\n(c) a rule that depends on a person being satisfied of one or more\nspecified matters;\n\n(d) rules for the making of applications for internal review, or of\napplications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview, of decisions of a person under the consumer data\nrules;\n\n(e) rules about the manner or form in which persons or bodies:\n\n(i) may exercise powers under the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) must comply with requirements imposed by the\nconsumer data rules;\n\nwhich could include requiring the use of a form approved by\nthe Commission or by the Information Commissioner;\n\n(f) rules about the following matters:\n\n(i) the manner in which CDR participants for CDR data\nmay charge (or cause to be charged) a fee for a matter\ncovered by the consumer data rules;\n\n(ii) the time for paying such a fee;\n\n(iii) giving notice of, or publicising, such a fee or matters\nabout such a fee;\n\n(g) rules requiring CDR participants, or designated gateways, for\nCDR data to have internal or external dispute resolution\nprocesses:\n\n(i) that relate to the operation of the consumer data rules or\nthis Part; and\n\n(ii) that meet specified criteria;\n\n(h) rules relating to an external dispute resolution scheme\nrecognised under Division 4, including about access to such a\nscheme;\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "Without limiting paragraph 56BB(f), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) rules that refer to the data standards;\n\n(b) the circumstances in which persons are, or may be, relieved\nfrom complying with requirements in the consumer data rules\nthat would otherwise apply to them;\n\n(c) a rule that depends on a person being satisfied of one or more\nspecified matters;\n\n(d) rules for the making of applications for internal review, or of\napplications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview, of decisions of a person under the consumer data\nrules;\n\n(e) rules about the manner or form in which persons or bodies:\n\n(i) may exercise powers under the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) must comply with requirements imposed by the\nconsumer data rules;\n\nwhich could include requiring the use of a form approved by\nthe Commission or by the Information Commissioner;\n\n(f) rules about the following matters:\n\n(i) the manner in which CDR participants for CDR data\nmay charge (or cause to be charged) a fee for a matter\ncovered by the consumer data rules;\n\n(ii) the time for paying such a fee;\n\n(iii) giving notice of, or publicising, such a fee or matters\nabout such a fee;\n\n(g) rules requiring CDR participants, or designated gateways, for\nCDR data to have internal or external dispute resolution\nprocesses:\n\n(i) that relate to the operation of the consumer data rules or\nthis Part; and\n\n(ii) that meet specified criteria;\n\n(h) rules relating to an external dispute resolution scheme\nrecognised under Division 4, including about access to such a\nscheme;\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bj-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7fbc637d99d128243c0839330074c4b442b7e542f0dd0edd62f06889bd0fce8e",
      "skos:note": "Rules about incidental or related matters"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BJ Rules about incidental or related matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "Without limiting paragraph 56BB(f), the consumer data rules may\ninclude the following rules:\n\n(a) rules that refer to the data standards;\n\n(b) the circumstances in which persons are, or may be, relieved\nfrom complying with requirements in the consumer data rules\nthat would otherwise apply to them;\n\n(c) a rule that depends on a person being satisfied of one or more\nspecified matters;\n\n(d) rules for the making of applications for internal review, or of\napplications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview, of decisions of a person under the consumer data\nrules;\n\n(e) rules about the manner or form in which persons or bodies:\n\n(i) may exercise powers under the consumer data rules; or\n\n(ii) must comply with requirements imposed by the\nconsumer data rules;\n\nwhich could include requiring the use of a form approved by\nthe Commission or by the Information Commissioner;\n\n(f) rules about the following matters:\n\n(i) the manner in which CDR participants for CDR data\nmay charge (or cause to be charged) a fee for a matter\ncovered by the consumer data rules;\n\n(ii) the time for paying such a fee;\n\n(iii) giving notice of, or publicising, such a fee or matters\nabout such a fee;\n\n(g) rules requiring CDR participants, or designated gateways, for\nCDR data to have internal or external dispute resolution\nprocesses:\n\n(i) that relate to the operation of the consumer data rules or\nthis Part; and\n\n(ii) that meet specified criteria;\n\n(h) rules relating to an external dispute resolution scheme\nrecognised under Division 4, including about access to such a\nscheme;\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bj-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bj"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BK Further limitations on the consumer data rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The consumer data rules cannot impose on a person a requirement\nthat has a retrospective commencement or application.\nExample: The rules cannot require a data holder to disclose CDR data on a day\nbefore the rules are registered, or on a day before the registration of a\nvariation to the rules that includes the requirement.\nNote:\nOther limitations on the consumer data rules are in sections 56BD,\n56BF and 56BG.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the consumer data rules may require a person to do\nsomething on a particular day, in relation to CDR data generated or\ncollected on an earlier day, if the person:\n\n(a) is a data holder of the CDR data; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person; or\n\n(c) is a person who has given a valid request under the consumer\ndata rules relating to the CDR data; or\n\n(d) is a designated gateway for the CDR data.\nExample: A data holder is given a valid request to disclose CDR data that was\ngenerated before the rules are registered. The rules can require that\ndisclosure.\n\n(3) The regulations may provide that the consumer data rules:\n\n(a) have no effect to the extent that the consumer data rules deal\nwith specified matters, or impose specified requirements, in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) specified classes of persons; or\n\n(b) only have effect to the extent that the consumer data rules\ndeal with specified matters, or impose specified\nrequirements, in relation to:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(ii) specified classes of persons.\nThe consumer data rules have effect (or no effect) accordingly.\n\n(4) Subsections (1) and (3) apply despite any other provision of this\nDivision.\nSubdivision B—Compliance with consumer data rules",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The consumer data rules cannot impose on a person a requirement\nthat has a retrospective commencement or application.\nExample: The rules cannot require a data holder to disclose CDR data on a day\nbefore the rules are registered, or on a day before the registration of a\nvariation to the rules that includes the requirement.\nNote:\nOther limitations on the consumer data rules are in sections 56BD,\n56BF and 56BG.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the consumer data rules may require a person to do\nsomething on a particular day, in relation to CDR data generated or\ncollected on an earlier day, if the person:\n\n(a) is a data holder of the CDR data; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person; or\n\n(c) is a person who has given a valid request under the consumer\ndata rules relating to the CDR data; or\n\n(d) is a designated gateway for the CDR data.\nExample: A data holder is given a valid request to disclose CDR data that was\ngenerated before the rules are registered. The rules can require that\ndisclosure.\n\n(3) The regulations may provide that the consumer data rules:\n\n(a) have no effect to the extent that the consumer data rules deal\nwith specified matters, or impose specified requirements, in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) specified classes of persons; or\n\n(b) only have effect to the extent that the consumer data rules\ndeal with specified matters, or impose specified\nrequirements, in relation to:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(ii) specified classes of persons.\nThe consumer data rules have effect (or no effect) accordingly.\n\n(4) Subsections (1) and (3) apply despite any other provision of this\nDivision.\nSubdivision B—Compliance with consumer data rules",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bk-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bk-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bk-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b70452f6d97ad0822cac28468aa347b962106d6a40046a4cf89ec07bcd392612"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BK Further limitations on the consumer data rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The consumer data rules cannot impose on a person a requirement\nthat has a retrospective commencement or application.\nExample: The rules cannot require a data holder to disclose CDR data on a day\nbefore the rules are registered, or on a day before the registration of a\nvariation to the rules that includes the requirement.\nNote:\nOther limitations on the consumer data rules are in sections 56BD,\n56BF and 56BG.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, the consumer data rules may require a person to do\nsomething on a particular day, in relation to CDR data generated or\ncollected on an earlier day, if the person:\n\n(a) is a data holder of the CDR data; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person; or\n\n(c) is a person who has given a valid request under the consumer\ndata rules relating to the CDR data; or\n\n(d) is a designated gateway for the CDR data.\nExample: A data holder is given a valid request to disclose CDR data that was\ngenerated before the rules are registered. The rules can require that\ndisclosure.\n\n(3) The regulations may provide that the consumer data rules:\n\n(a) have no effect to the extent that the consumer data rules deal\nwith specified matters, or impose specified requirements, in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) specified classes of persons; or\n\n(b) only have effect to the extent that the consumer data rules\ndeal with specified matters, or impose specified\nrequirements, in relation to:\n\n(i) specified classes of CDR data; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(ii) specified classes of persons.\nThe consumer data rules have effect (or no effect) accordingly.\n\n(4) Subsections (1) and (3) apply despite any other provision of this\nDivision.\nSubdivision B—Compliance with consumer data rules"
    },
    {
