    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BQ Commission to consult before making the rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making consumer data rules under subsection 56BA(1), the\nCommission must:\n\n(a) consult the public about the making of the rules:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that includes making information\navailable on the Commission’s website, and inviting the\npublic to comment; and\n\n(b) consult each of the following about the making of the rules:\n\n(i) the Information Commissioner;\n\n(ii) if the rules relate to a particular designated sector—the\nperson or body (if any) that the Commission believes to\nbe the primary regulator of that sector;\n\n(iii) any person or body prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(c) wait at least 60 days after the day consultation of the public\nbegins under paragraph (a) about the making of the rules.\n\n(2) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not invalidate the\nconsumer data rules.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before making consumer data rules under subsection 56BA(1), the\nCommission must:\n\n(a) consult the public about the making of the rules:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that includes making information\navailable on the Commission’s website, and inviting the\npublic to comment; and\n\n(b) consult each of the following about the making of the rules:\n\n(i) the Information Commissioner;\n\n(ii) if the rules relate to a particular designated sector—the\nperson or body (if any) that the Commission believes to\nbe the primary regulator of that sector;\n\n(iii) any person or body prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(c) wait at least 60 days after the day consultation of the public\nbegins under paragraph (a) about the making of the rules.\n\n(2) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not invalidate the\nconsumer data rules.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bq-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "11f36841c2ecaaf923256195ff32e899c6d16d5d7b2103f4470fb422903e415f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BQ Commission to consult before making the rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making consumer data rules under subsection 56BA(1), the\nCommission must:\n\n(a) consult the public about the making of the rules:\n\n(i) for at least 28 days; and\n\n(ii) in one or more ways that includes making information\navailable on the Commission’s website, and inviting the\npublic to comment; and\n\n(b) consult each of the following about the making of the rules:\n\n(i) the Information Commissioner;\n\n(ii) if the rules relate to a particular designated sector—the\nperson or body (if any) that the Commission believes to\nbe the primary regulator of that sector;\n\n(iii) any person or body prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(c) wait at least 60 days after the day consultation of the public\nbegins under paragraph (a) about the making of the rules.\n\n(2) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not invalidate the\nconsumer data rules."
    },
