    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56br",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BR Ministerial consent to rules required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56br"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "The Commission must not make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1) unless the Minister has consented, in writing,\nto the making of the rules.\nNote:\nIn an emergency, consent is not required (see section 56BS).\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019",
      "skos:definition": "The Commission must not make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1) unless the Minister has consented, in writing,\nto the making of the rules.\nNote:\nIn an emergency, consent is not required (see section 56BS).\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56br-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56br-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "01d753326b02f2b4c20d47e7aa7a0d2276f41b08f9cf72ab4a47a1fb9879e9bd",
      "skos:note": "Ministerial consent required for consumer data rules"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56br",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BR Ministerial consent to rules required",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "The Commission must not make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1) unless the Minister has consented, in writing,\nto the making of the rules.\nNote:\nIn an emergency, consent is not required (see section 56BS).\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56br-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56br"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56br-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires ministerial consent",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BS Emergency rules: usual consultation and consent not required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bs"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1):\n\n(a) after consulting the Information Commissioner, but without\notherwise complying with section 56BQ; and\n\n(b) without the consent of the Minister as required by\nsection 56BR;\nif the Commission believes (whether or not that belief is\nreasonable) that it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of\nserious harm to:\n\n(c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the\nAustralian economy; or\n\n(d) the interests of consumers.\nNote:\nThe Commission still needs to comply with section 56BP.\n\n(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(a) does not\ninvalidate rules made as described in subsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see subsection 56BT(3)).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1):\n\n(a) after consulting the Information Commissioner, but without\notherwise complying with section 56BQ; and\n\n(b) without the consent of the Minister as required by\nsection 56BR;\nif the Commission believes (whether or not that belief is\nreasonable) that it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of\nserious harm to:\n\n(c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the\nAustralian economy; or\n\n(d) the interests of consumers.\nNote:\nThe Commission still needs to comply with section 56BP.\n\n(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(a) does not\ninvalidate rules made as described in subsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see subsection 56BT(3)).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cff3c5396a0cfd6aa670e6742397c7ddc80442f11c83efbb9387063b27c1b536"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bs",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BS Emergency rules: usual consultation and consent not required",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may make consumer data rules under\nsubsection 56BA(1):\n\n(a) after consulting the Information Commissioner, but without\notherwise complying with section 56BQ; and\n\n(b) without the consent of the Minister as required by\nsection 56BR;\nif the Commission believes (whether or not that belief is\nreasonable) that it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of\nserious harm to:\n\n(c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the\nAustralian economy; or\n\n(d) the interests of consumers.\nNote:\nThe Commission still needs to comply with section 56BP.\n\n(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(a) does not\ninvalidate rules made as described in subsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see subsection 56BT(3))."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BS(1) Emergency rules: usual consultation and consent not required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-1"
      },
