        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7adc5c93affad2ce7fdb281701e64770d9164b5a47ffbb0fe4978cc891747d8",
      "skos:note": "No obligation to comply with paragraph (1)(a) if rules made under subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BS(2) Emergency rules: usual consultation and consent not required",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(a) does not\ninvalidate rules made as described in subsection (1).\nNote:\nSuch rules may have a limited life (see subsection 56BT(3))."
    },
    {
