    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BT Emergency rules: consequences if made",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission makes consumer data rules as described in\nsubsection 56BS(1) (the emergency rules), the Commission must:\n\n(a) on the following day, give the Minister a written explanation\nof the need for the emergency rules; and\n\n(b) vary or repeal the emergency rules in accordance with any\ndirections given under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, direct the Commission to vary or\nrepeal the emergency rules.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the emergency rules are made without consulting the\nInformation Commissioner, but otherwise in accordance with\nsubsection 56BS(1); and\n\n(b) the Minister does not give a direction under subsection (2)\nabout the emergency rules;\nthe emergency rules cease to be in force 6 months after the day\nthey are made.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission makes consumer data rules as described in\nsubsection 56BS(1) (the emergency rules), the Commission must:\n\n(a) on the following day, give the Minister a written explanation\nof the need for the emergency rules; and\n\n(b) vary or repeal the emergency rules in accordance with any\ndirections given under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, direct the Commission to vary or\nrepeal the emergency rules.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the emergency rules are made without consulting the\nInformation Commissioner, but otherwise in accordance with\nsubsection 56BS(1); and\n\n(b) the Minister does not give a direction under subsection (2)\nabout the emergency rules;\nthe emergency rules cease to be in force 6 months after the day\nthey are made.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bt-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bt-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bt-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37ebd5757f7139985745d1c5993b3782412aac700b8b4f53f0946c83d80c62f9"
    },
