    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bv",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BV Commission may intervene if fee for disclosing or using",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bv"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc.\n\n(1) The Commission may determine the following for a specified CDR\nparticipant for specified chargeable CDR data:\n\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure;\n\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (3).\n\n(2) When determining an amount or method under subsection (1), the\nCommission must seek to ensure that the resulting fee:\n\n(a) reflects the reasonable costs (including capital costs)\nnecessary for the CDR participant to comply with this Part\nand the consumer data rules in relation to the chargeable\nmatters; and\n\n(b) is reasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (3).\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc.\n\n(1) The Commission may determine the following for a specified CDR\nparticipant for specified chargeable CDR data:\n\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure;\n\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (3).\n\n(2) When determining an amount or method under subsection (1), the\nCommission must seek to ensure that the resulting fee:\n\n(a) reflects the reasonable costs (including capital costs)\nnecessary for the CDR participant to comply with this Part\nand the consumer data rules in relation to the chargeable\nmatters; and\n\n(b) is reasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (3).\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bv-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bv-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0dc0f7a1f0343c1249dbcd2b2483f5f5793c8b543ccf0889e8cccd706b2b03f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bv",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BV Commission may intervene if fee for disclosing or using",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "chargeable CDR data is unreasonable etc.\n\n(1) The Commission may determine the following for a specified CDR\nparticipant for specified chargeable CDR data:\n\n(a) the amount of a fee, or a method for working out the amount\nof a fee, that the CDR participant may charge (or cause to be\ncharged) for either or both of the following matters (the\nchargeable matters):\n\n(i) the disclosure of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances because of a requirement under the\nconsumer data rules to do so;\n\n(ii) the use of the chargeable CDR data in chargeable\ncircumstances as the result of such a disclosure;\n\n(b) the specified persons who are liable to pay that fee;\nif the Commission is satisfied that the fee that the CDR participant\nwould otherwise charge (or cause to be charged) is unreasonable\nhaving regard to the criteria in subsection (3).\n\n(2) When determining an amount or method under subsection (1), the\nCommission must seek to ensure that the resulting fee:\n\n(a) reflects the reasonable costs (including capital costs)\nnecessary for the CDR participant to comply with this Part\nand the consumer data rules in relation to the chargeable\nmatters; and\n\n(b) is reasonable having regard to the criteria in subsection (3).\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
    {
