    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56BX Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bx"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a determination made under subsection 56BV(1),\nthe Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the\ndetermination; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying such\na determination is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than\nsections 56BW to 56BY)) to be a determination of the\nCommission.\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to\ngive such information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nCommission in connection with the making of the determination to\nwhich the review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On a review of a determination made under subsection 56BV(1),\nthe Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the\ndetermination; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying such\na determination is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than\nsections 56BW to 56BY)) to be a determination of the\nCommission.\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to\ngive such information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nCommission in connection with the making of the determination to\nwhich the review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "881e632501678d6f11066905409604bd72ee2c9a9cf0b989b7180b6d751be9cc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56bx",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56BX Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a determination made under subsection 56BV(1),\nthe Tribunal:\n\n(a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the\ndetermination; and\n\n(b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions\nand exercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying such\na determination is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than\nsections 56BW to 56BY)) to be a determination of the\nCommission.\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to\ngive such information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nCommission in connection with the making of the determination to\nwhich the review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal."
    },
