        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CC Prohibition on holding out—offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person holds out that the\nperson:\n\n(a) is an accredited person; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person holding an accreditation that has been\ngranted at a particular level (see paragraph 56BH(1)(d)); or\n\n(c) is an accredited data recipient of CDR data;\nif that is not the case.\nPenalty—body corporate\n\n(2) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate\nis punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater\nof the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the annual turnover of the body corporate during the\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncommission of the offence happened or began.\n\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(c), annual turnover has the\nsame meaning as in Division 1 of Part IV.\nPenalty—other persons\n\n(4) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a person other\nthan a body corporate is punishable on conviction by imprisonment\nfor not more than 5 years, a fine of not more than $500,000, or\nboth.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person holds out that the\nperson:\n\n(a) is an accredited person; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person holding an accreditation that has been\ngranted at a particular level (see paragraph 56BH(1)(d)); or\n\n(c) is an accredited data recipient of CDR data;\nif that is not the case.\nPenalty—body corporate\n\n(2) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate\nis punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater\nof the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the annual turnover of the body corporate during the\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncommission of the offence happened or began.\n\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(c), annual turnover has the\nsame meaning as in Division 1 of Part IV.\nPenalty—other persons\n\n(4) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a person other\nthan a body corporate is punishable on conviction by imprisonment\nfor not more than 5 years, a fine of not more than $500,000, or\nboth.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2952d34c34f4fca327e27b31f1f7064d3a21a66b1e8976c8ca49333ce5e4bec3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CC Prohibition on holding out—offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if the person holds out that the\nperson:\n\n(a) is an accredited person; or\n\n(b) is an accredited person holding an accreditation that has been\ngranted at a particular level (see paragraph 56BH(1)(d)); or\n\n(c) is an accredited data recipient of CDR data;\nif that is not the case.\nPenalty—body corporate\n\n(2) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate\nis punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater\nof the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the annual turnover of the body corporate during the\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncommission of the offence happened or began.\n\n(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(c), annual turnover has the\nsame meaning as in Division 1 of Part IV.\nPenalty—other persons\n\n(4) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a person other\nthan a body corporate is punishable on conviction by imprisonment\nfor not more than 5 years, a fine of not more than $500,000, or\nboth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-1",
