    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CC(2) Prohibition on holding out—offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate\nis punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater\nof the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the annual turnover of the body corporate during the\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncommission of the offence happened or began.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate\nis punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater\nof the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the annual turnover of the body corporate during the\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncommission of the offence happened or began.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "05de0ca698eb6d96e8d8f9f2fc17168fb97452540a57e1fa782ab21f6e3bd3d4",
      "skos:note": "Offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate is punishable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cc-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CC(2) Prohibition on holding out—offence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An offence against subsection (1) committed by a body corporate\nis punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than the greater\nof the following:\n\n(a) $10,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the commission of the offence—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—10%\nof the annual turnover of the body corporate during the\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n12-month period ending at the end of the month in which the\ncommission of the offence happened or began."
    },
