    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CG Appointment of the Data Recipient Accreditor",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the Data\nRecipient Accreditor a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe Commission will be the Data Recipient Accreditor in the absence\nof an appointment under this subsection (see the definition of Data\nRecipient Accreditor in subsection 4(1)).\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the Data\nRecipient Accreditor a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe Commission will be the Data Recipient Accreditor in the absence\nof an appointment under this subsection (see the definition of Data\nRecipient Accreditor in subsection 4(1)).\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af4ea3feb7b485d9db3c2206cded6a1102d3af722a5eef13830c47407312656b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CG Appointment of the Data Recipient Accreditor",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint as the Data\nRecipient Accreditor a person who:\n\n(a) is the accountable authority of a Commonwealth entity\n(within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013); or\n\n(b) is a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of that Act).\nNote 1:\nFor variation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nThe Commission will be the Data Recipient Accreditor in the absence\nof an appointment under this subsection (see the definition of Data\nRecipient Accreditor in subsection 4(1)).\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by written instrument, terminate an\nappointment made under subsection (1)."
    },
