    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CH Functions, powers and annual report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ch"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Data Recipient Accreditor are:\n\n(a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(2) The Data Recipient Accreditor has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Data Recipient Accreditor,\nboth:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the Data Recipient Accreditor (their primary capacity);\nand\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the Data Recipient\nAccreditor while the person is the Data Recipient Accreditor.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the Data Recipient Accreditor at any time during a\nperiod; and\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of\nthe Data Recipient Accreditor’s powers, at that time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The functions of the Data Recipient Accreditor are:\n\n(a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(2) The Data Recipient Accreditor has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Data Recipient Accreditor,\nboth:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the Data Recipient Accreditor (their primary capacity);\nand\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the Data Recipient\nAccreditor while the person is the Data Recipient Accreditor.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the Data Recipient Accreditor at any time during a\nperiod; and\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of\nthe Data Recipient Accreditor’s powers, at that time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b323c42aec8dde0a816c8dc5ff86af19a2dcdf4f2fb00b06aac6d13408f9a8b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ch",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CH Functions, powers and annual report",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Data Recipient Accreditor are:\n\n(a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(2) The Data Recipient Accreditor has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Data Recipient Accreditor,\nboth:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the Data Recipient Accreditor (their primary capacity);\nand\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the Data Recipient\nAccreditor while the person is the Data Recipient Accreditor.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the Data Recipient Accreditor at any time during a\nperiod; and\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of\nthe Data Recipient Accreditor’s powers, at that time."
    },
