    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56CL Functions, powers and annual report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Accreditation Registrar are:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(a) those described in Subdivision B; and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) The Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Accreditation Registrar’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Accreditation Registrar,\nboth:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the Accreditation Registrar (their primary capacity); and\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the Accreditation\nRegistrar while the person is the Accreditation Registrar.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the Accreditation Registrar at any time during a\nperiod; and\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the Accreditation Registrar’s functions, and the exercise of the\nAccreditation Registrar’s powers, at that time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The functions of the Accreditation Registrar are:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(a) those described in Subdivision B; and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) The Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Accreditation Registrar’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Accreditation Registrar,\nboth:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the Accreditation Registrar (their primary capacity); and\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the Accreditation\nRegistrar while the person is the Accreditation Registrar.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the Accreditation Registrar at any time during a\nperiod; and\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the Accreditation Registrar’s functions, and the exercise of the\nAccreditation Registrar’s powers, at that time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cl-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cl-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56cl-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d2bf1edba03fa6493b67972f1c4489eca0a2d062ed9539dbb22f3f25f812cc2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56cl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56CL Functions, powers and annual report",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Accreditation Registrar are:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(a) those described in Subdivision B; and\n\n(b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data\nrules.\n\n(2) The Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all other things\nnecessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the\nperformance of the Accreditation Registrar’s functions.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Accreditation Registrar,\nboth:\n\n(a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than\nas the Accreditation Registrar (their primary capacity); and\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may\nbe performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by\nanyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the\nperson in that primary capacity;\nare taken to include the functions and powers of the Accreditation\nRegistrar while the person is the Accreditation Registrar.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a person is the Accreditation Registrar at any time during a\nperiod; and\n\n(b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46\nof the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability\nAct 2013:\n\n(i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or\n\n(ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity;\nthe annual report must include information about the performance\nof the Accreditation Registrar’s functions, and the exercise of the\nAccreditation Registrar’s powers, at that time."
    },
