    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ec-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EC(4) Relationship with other laws",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ec-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite the Privacy Act 1988:\n\n(a) the Australian Privacy Principles do not apply to an\naccredited data recipient of CDR data in relation to the CDR\ndata; and\n\n(b) if subsection 56EN(1) applies to a disclosure of CDR data by\na data holder of the CDR data—Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 10 does not apply to the data holder in relation to\nthat disclosure of the CDR data; and\n\n(c) if subsection 56EP(1) applies to CDR data and a data holder\nof the CDR data—Australian Privacy Principle 13 does not\napply to the data holder in relation to the CDR data; and\n\n(d) Australian Privacy Principles 6, 7 and 11 do not apply to a\ndesignated gateway for CDR data in relation to the CDR\ndata.\nNote 1:\nFor the accredited data recipient, the privacy safeguards will apply\ninstead.\nNote 2:\nSection 56EN (or privacy safeguard 11) is about the quality of CDR\ndata. Section 56EP (or privacy safeguard 13) is about correcting CDR\ndata.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite the Privacy Act 1988:\n\n(a) the Australian Privacy Principles do not apply to an\naccredited data recipient of CDR data in relation to the CDR\ndata; and\n\n(b) if subsection 56EN(1) applies to a disclosure of CDR data by\na data holder of the CDR data—Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 10 does not apply to the data holder in relation to\nthat disclosure of the CDR data; and\n\n(c) if subsection 56EP(1) applies to CDR data and a data holder\nof the CDR data—Australian Privacy Principle 13 does not\napply to the data holder in relation to the CDR data; and\n\n(d) Australian Privacy Principles 6, 7 and 11 do not apply to a\ndesignated gateway for CDR data in relation to the CDR\ndata.\nNote 1:\nFor the accredited data recipient, the privacy safeguards will apply\ninstead.\nNote 2:\nSection 56EN (or privacy safeguard 11) is about the quality of CDR\ndata. Section 56EP (or privacy safeguard 13) is about correcting CDR\ndata.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ec"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ec-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ec-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37dba11fecf02c9e6b7a8c39513464fda7db240fab0788c6ef57fd24df0bd777",
      "skos:note": "Exempts accredited data recipients from Australian Privacy Principles"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ec-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EC(4) Relationship with other laws",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite the Privacy Act 1988:\n\n(a) the Australian Privacy Principles do not apply to an\naccredited data recipient of CDR data in relation to the CDR\ndata; and\n\n(b) if subsection 56EN(1) applies to a disclosure of CDR data by\na data holder of the CDR data—Australian Privacy\nPrinciple 10 does not apply to the data holder in relation to\nthat disclosure of the CDR data; and\n\n(c) if subsection 56EP(1) applies to CDR data and a data holder\nof the CDR data—Australian Privacy Principle 13 does not\napply to the data holder in relation to the CDR data; and\n\n(d) Australian Privacy Principles 6, 7 and 11 do not apply to a\ndesignated gateway for CDR data in relation to the CDR\ndata.\nNote 1:\nFor the accredited data recipient, the privacy safeguards will apply\ninstead.\nNote 2:\nSection 56EN (or privacy safeguard 11) is about the quality of CDR\ndata. Section 56EP (or privacy safeguard 13) is about correcting CDR\ndata."
    },
