    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56ED(5) Privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited data recipient of any CDR data,\nthe CDR entity’s policy must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the classes of CDR data held by (or on behalf of) the CDR\nentity as an accredited data recipient, and how such CDR\ndata is held;\n\n(b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use\nor disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data;\n\n(c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the\nCDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;\n\n(d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain\nabout a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or\nthe consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal\nwith such a complaint;\n\n(e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data\nto accredited persons who are based overseas;\n\n(f) if the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data to\naccredited persons who are based overseas—the countries in\nwhich such persons are likely to be based if it is practicable\nto specify those countries in the policy;\n\n(g) the circumstances in which the CDR entity may disclose such\nCDR data to a person who is not an accredited person;\n\n(h) the events about which the CDR entity will notify the CDR\nconsumers of such CDR data;\n\n(i) the circumstances in which the CDR entity must delete or\nde-identify such CDR data in accordance with a request\ngiven by a CDR consumer for the CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited data recipient of any CDR data,\nthe CDR entity’s policy must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the classes of CDR data held by (or on behalf of) the CDR\nentity as an accredited data recipient, and how such CDR\ndata is held;\n\n(b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use\nor disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data;\n\n(c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the\nCDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;\n\n(d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain\nabout a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or\nthe consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal\nwith such a complaint;\n\n(e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data\nto accredited persons who are based overseas;\n\n(f) if the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data to\naccredited persons who are based overseas—the countries in\nwhich such persons are likely to be based if it is practicable\nto specify those countries in the policy;\n\n(g) the circumstances in which the CDR entity may disclose such\nCDR data to a person who is not an accredited person;\n\n(h) the events about which the CDR entity will notify the CDR\nconsumers of such CDR data;\n\n(i) the circumstances in which the CDR entity must delete or\nde-identify such CDR data in accordance with a request\ngiven by a CDR consumer for the CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fcdbb4e8f8072a0f7a1c11722a26fbedbc7e73e08536a66b0f616f0db61c8851",
      "skos:note": "CDR entity must provide specific information about CDR data",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56ED(5) Privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited data recipient of any CDR data,\nthe CDR entity’s policy must contain the following information:\n\n(a) the classes of CDR data held by (or on behalf of) the CDR\nentity as an accredited data recipient, and how such CDR\ndata is held;\n\n(b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use\nor disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data;\n\n(c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the\nCDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;\n\n(d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain\nabout a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or\nthe consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal\nwith such a complaint;\n\n(e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data\nto accredited persons who are based overseas;\n\n(f) if the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data to\naccredited persons who are based overseas—the countries in\nwhich such persons are likely to be based if it is practicable\nto specify those countries in the policy;\n\n(g) the circumstances in which the CDR entity may disclose such\nCDR data to a person who is not an accredited person;\n\n(h) the events about which the CDR entity will notify the CDR\nconsumers of such CDR data;\n\n(i) the circumstances in which the CDR entity must delete or\nde-identify such CDR data in accordance with a request\ngiven by a CDR consumer for the CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules."
    },
