    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ee",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EE Privacy safeguard 2—anonymity and pseudonymity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ee"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must give each CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data the option of using a pseudonym, or\nnot identifying themselves, when dealing with the accredited data\nrecipient in relation to the CDR data.\nNote:\nThe CDR participant from whom the accredited data recipient\nacquired the CDR data may be subject to a similar obligation under\nAustralian Privacy Principle 2.\n\n(2) That option may be given to a CDR consumer for the CDR data\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances specified in the\nconsumer data rules.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nSubdivision C—Collecting CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must give each CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data the option of using a pseudonym, or\nnot identifying themselves, when dealing with the accredited data\nrecipient in relation to the CDR data.\nNote:\nThe CDR participant from whom the accredited data recipient\nacquired the CDR data may be subject to a similar obligation under\nAustralian Privacy Principle 2.\n\n(2) That option may be given to a CDR consumer for the CDR data\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances specified in the\nconsumer data rules.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nSubdivision C—Collecting CDR data",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ee-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ee-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ee-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d76cb491e7362eb97343f612aaca0006393d199454059f8e8b4edb022ddc36b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ee",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EE Privacy safeguard 2—anonymity and pseudonymity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must give each CDR\nconsumer for the CDR data the option of using a pseudonym, or\nnot identifying themselves, when dealing with the accredited data\nrecipient in relation to the CDR data.\nNote:\nThe CDR participant from whom the accredited data recipient\nacquired the CDR data may be subject to a similar obligation under\nAustralian Privacy Principle 2.\n\n(2) That option may be given to a CDR consumer for the CDR data\nthrough a designated gateway for the CDR data.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances specified in the\nconsumer data rules.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nSubdivision C—Collecting CDR data"
    },
