    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ef",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from CDR",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ef"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "participants\n\n(1) An accredited person must not seek to collect CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules from a CDR participant for the CDR data\nunless:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has requested this by\ngiving a valid request under the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) the person complies with all other requirements in the\nconsumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from\nthe CDR participant.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the\nCDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a\ndesignated gateway for the CDR data.\nNote:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (1)(a) could be given\nthrough a designated gateway (see section 56BG).",
      "skos:definition": "participants\n\n(1) An accredited person must not seek to collect CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules from a CDR participant for the CDR data\nunless:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has requested this by\ngiving a valid request under the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) the person complies with all other requirements in the\nconsumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from\nthe CDR participant.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the\nCDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a\ndesignated gateway for the CDR data.\nNote:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (1)(a) could be given\nthrough a designated gateway (see section 56BG).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ef-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ef-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34ef94a0ea333af91dd061f0a4f5a567f6a924e1bbee5fb4f3a4131192e4261a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ef",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from CDR",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "participants\n\n(1) An accredited person must not seek to collect CDR data under the\nconsumer data rules from a CDR participant for the CDR data\nunless:\n\n(a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has requested this by\ngiving a valid request under the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) the person complies with all other requirements in the\nconsumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from\nthe CDR participant.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the\nCDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a\ndesignated gateway for the CDR data.\nNote:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (1)(a) could be given\nthrough a designated gateway (see section 56BG)."
    },
