    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EG Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56eg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "CDR participants\n\n(1) If a person:\n\n(a) while the person is an accredited person, collects CDR data\nfrom a CDR participant for the CDR data:\n\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect that CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order;\nthe person must destroy that CDR data as soon as practicable.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the\nCDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a\ndesignated gateway for the CDR data.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "CDR participants\n\n(1) If a person:\n\n(a) while the person is an accredited person, collects CDR data\nfrom a CDR participant for the CDR data:\n\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect that CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order;\nthe person must destroy that CDR data as soon as practicable.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the\nCDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a\ndesignated gateway for the CDR data.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85c775ae15a55934615f561c2fb4dfeb002ce28caf83fcc042b25372867e5002"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56eg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EG Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "CDR participants\n\n(1) If a person:\n\n(a) while the person is an accredited person, collects CDR data\nfrom a CDR participant for the CDR data:\n\n(i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but\n\n(ii) not as the result of seeking to collect that CDR data\nunder the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an\nAustralian law or a court/tribunal order;\nthe person must destroy that CDR data as soon as practicable.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the\nCDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a\ndesignated gateway for the CDR data.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
