    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EH Privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56eh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "If a person collects CDR data in accordance with section 56EF, the\nperson must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the collection; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis section is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nSubdivision D—Dealing with CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "If a person collects CDR data in accordance with section 56EF, the\nperson must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the collection; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis section is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nSubdivision D—Dealing with CDR data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eh-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eh-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28c9bf5a37e553be0a5c5bb9c1153529b8fc4029775dd531c6a1dd4cd732cdb6",
      "skos:note": "Notify CDR consumers of collection of CDR data",
      "dc:description": "Notification of CDR consumer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56eh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EH Privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "If a person collects CDR data in accordance with section 56EF, the\nperson must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the collection; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis section is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nSubdivision D—Dealing with CDR data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eh-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eh"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eh-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide notification",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ei",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EI Privacy safeguard 6—use or disclosure of CDR data by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ei"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "accredited data recipients or designated gateways\n\n(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must not use or disclose\nit unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules in response to a valid request from a\nCDR consumer for the CDR data; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is otherwise required, or authorised,\nunder the consumer data rules; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) another Australian law; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order;\n\nand the accredited data recipient makes a written note of the\nuse or disclosure.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (a) could be given through a\ndesignated gateway (see section 56BG).\nNote 3:\nThe Australian Privacy Principles will not apply for\nsubparagraph (c)(i) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a)).\n\n(2) A designated gateway for CDR data must not use or disclose it\nunless:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is authorised under the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) another Australian law; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order;\n\nand the designated gateway makes a written note of the use\nor disclosure in accordance with the consumer data rules.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 6 will not apply for subparagraph (c)(i)\n(see paragraph 56EC(4)(d)).\n\n(3) Neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies to the use or disclosure of\nCDR data for the purposes of direct marketing.\nNote:\nSection 56EJ deals with the use or disclosure of CDR data for the\npurposes of direct marketing.",
      "skos:definition": "accredited data recipients or designated gateways\n\n(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must not use or disclose\nit unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules in response to a valid request from a\nCDR consumer for the CDR data; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is otherwise required, or authorised,\nunder the consumer data rules; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) another Australian law; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order;\n\nand the accredited data recipient makes a written note of the\nuse or disclosure.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (a) could be given through a\ndesignated gateway (see section 56BG).\nNote 3:\nThe Australian Privacy Principles will not apply for\nsubparagraph (c)(i) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a)).\n\n(2) A designated gateway for CDR data must not use or disclose it\nunless:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is authorised under the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) another Australian law; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order;\n\nand the designated gateway makes a written note of the use\nor disclosure in accordance with the consumer data rules.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 6 will not apply for subparagraph (c)(i)\n(see paragraph 56EC(4)(d)).\n\n(3) Neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies to the use or disclosure of\nCDR data for the purposes of direct marketing.\nNote:\nSection 56EJ deals with the use or disclosure of CDR data for the\npurposes of direct marketing.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ei-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ei-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ei-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f17e691747e6cd13fd9731ea0288bdf762bc2acb6dfb2b95e24c018df66134e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ei",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EI Privacy safeguard 6—use or disclosure of CDR data by",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "accredited data recipients or designated gateways\n\n(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must not use or disclose\nit unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules in response to a valid request from a\nCDR consumer for the CDR data; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is otherwise required, or authorised,\nunder the consumer data rules; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) another Australian law; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order;\n\nand the accredited data recipient makes a written note of the\nuse or disclosure.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (a) could be given through a\ndesignated gateway (see section 56BG).\nNote 3:\nThe Australian Privacy Principles will not apply for\nsubparagraph (c)(i) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a)).\n\n(2) A designated gateway for CDR data must not use or disclose it\nunless:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is authorised under the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(c) the use or disclosure is required or authorised by or under:\n\n(i) another Australian law; or\n\n(ii) a court/tribunal order;\n\nand the designated gateway makes a written note of the use\nor disclosure in accordance with the consumer data rules.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 6 will not apply for subparagraph (c)(i)\n(see paragraph 56EC(4)(d)).\n\n(3) Neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies to the use or disclosure of\nCDR data for the purposes of direct marketing.\nNote:\nSection 56EJ deals with the use or disclosure of CDR data for the\npurposes of direct marketing."
    },
    {
