      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ej",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EJ Privacy safeguard 7—use or disclosure of CDR data for direct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ej"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "marketing by accredited data recipients or designated\ngateways\n\n(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must not use or disclose\nit for direct marketing unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules in response to a valid request from a\nCDR consumer for the CDR data; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is authorised under the consumer data\nrules in accordance with a valid consent of a CDR consumer\nfor the CDR data.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (a), or the valid consent\nreferred to in paragraph (b), could be given through a designated\ngateway (see section 56BG).\n\n(2) A designated gateway for CDR data must not use or disclose it for\ndirect marketing unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules; or\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "marketing by accredited data recipients or designated\ngateways\n\n(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must not use or disclose\nit for direct marketing unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules in response to a valid request from a\nCDR consumer for the CDR data; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is authorised under the consumer data\nrules in accordance with a valid consent of a CDR consumer\nfor the CDR data.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (a), or the valid consent\nreferred to in paragraph (b), could be given through a designated\ngateway (see section 56BG).\n\n(2) A designated gateway for CDR data must not use or disclose it for\ndirect marketing unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules; or\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ej-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ej-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9dfb97ba87d26e8576800c65f748351f0b93b5e28516a3f37209301996c9213d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ej",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EJ Privacy safeguard 7—use or disclosure of CDR data for direct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "marketing by accredited data recipients or designated\ngateways\n\n(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must not use or disclose\nit for direct marketing unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules in response to a valid request from a\nCDR consumer for the CDR data; or\n\n(b) the use or disclosure is authorised under the consumer data\nrules in accordance with a valid consent of a CDR consumer\nfor the CDR data.\nNote 1:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\nNote 2:\nThe valid request referred to in paragraph (a), or the valid consent\nreferred to in paragraph (b), could be given through a designated\ngateway (see section 56BG).\n\n(2) A designated gateway for CDR data must not use or disclose it for\ndirect marketing unless:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure—the disclosure is required under\nthe consumer data rules; or\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
