    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56el-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits disclosure of CDR data",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data proposes to disclose the CDR data;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "disclosure of CDR data without consent is prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56el-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "During",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Disclosures are only permitted during the period of accreditation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data proposes to disclose the CDR data;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "disclosure of CDR data without consent occurs outside the period of accreditation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56el-ss-2-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Disclosures are only permitted until the end of accreditation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data proposes to disclose the CDR data;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "disclosure of CDR data without consent occurs after the end of accreditation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56el-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Through",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Disclosures are only permitted through accredited recipients",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data proposes to disclose the CDR data;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "disclosure of CDR data without consent occurs through unauthorized recipients"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56el-ss-2-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "By",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Disclosures are only permitted by accredited recipients",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If a person who is an accredited data recipient of CDR data proposes to disclose the CDR data;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "disclosure of CDR data without consent occurs through unauthorized agents"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56em",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EM Privacy safeguard 10—notifying of the disclosure of CDR",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56em"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "data\n\n(1) If a data holder of CDR data is required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data to a person, the data\nholder must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data discloses the CDR data,\nthe accredited data recipient must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) or (2) applies even if the disclosure\nof the CDR data is to a designated gateway for the CDR data as\nrequired or authorised under the consumer data rules.\nNote:\nThe designated gateway may be subject to a similar notification\nrequirement under the consumer data rules (see\nparagraph 56BG(1)(c)).\nSubdivision E—Integrity of CDR data",
      "skos:definition": "data\n\n(1) If a data holder of CDR data is required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data to a person, the data\nholder must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data discloses the CDR data,\nthe accredited data recipient must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) or (2) applies even if the disclosure\nof the CDR data is to a designated gateway for the CDR data as\nrequired or authorised under the consumer data rules.\nNote:\nThe designated gateway may be subject to a similar notification\nrequirement under the consumer data rules (see\nparagraph 56BG(1)(c)).\nSubdivision E—Integrity of CDR data",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56em-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56em-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56em-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3a6eb0790f39ac87c94f3856b2dd2c5d110e6811602261a9a923d3bb23adc8b7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56em",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EM Privacy safeguard 10—notifying of the disclosure of CDR",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "data\n\n(1) If a data holder of CDR data is required or authorised under the\nconsumer data rules to disclose the CDR data to a person, the data\nholder must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data discloses the CDR data,\nthe accredited data recipient must:\n\n(a) take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to notify\nCDR consumers for the CDR data of the disclosure; and\n\n(b) ensure that this notification:\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(i) is given to those of the CDR consumers (if there are\nmore than one) that the consumer data rules require to\nbe notified; and\n\n(ii) covers the matters specified in those rules; and\n\n(iii) is given at or before the time specified in those rules.\nNote:\nThis subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) or (2) applies even if the disclosure\nof the CDR data is to a designated gateway for the CDR data as\nrequired or authorised under the consumer data rules.\nNote:\nThe designated gateway may be subject to a similar notification\nrequirement under the consumer data rules (see\nparagraph 56BG(1)(c)).\nSubdivision E—Integrity of CDR data"
    },
