          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56es-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56es-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb2322ce858cf6394d4e10ea342508175cd982f6698447482868662ce936a730",
      "skos:note": "Applicable provisions of the Privacy Act 1988 also apply to accredited data recipients and designated gateways for CDR data."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56es-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56ES(2) Notification of CDR data security breaches",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Part IIIC of the Privacy Act 1988, and any other provision of that\nAct that relates to that Part, also apply in relation to:\n\n(a) an accredited data recipient of CDR data; or\n\n(b) a designated gateway for CDR data;\nas if the substitutions in the following table, and the modifications\nin subsection (3), were made.\n\nSubstitutions to be made\nItem\nFor a reference in Part IIIC to …\n… substitute a reference to …\nany of the following:\n(a) personal information;\n(b) information\nCDR data.\nany of the following:\n(a) entity;\n(b) APP entity;\n(c) APP entity, credit reporting\nbody, credit provider or file\nnumber recipient, as the case\neach of the following:\n(a) accredited data recipient;\n(b) designated gateway.\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nSubstitutions to be made\nItem\nFor a reference in Part IIIC to …\n… substitute a reference to …\nmay be\nany of the following:\n(a) individual to whom information\nrelates;\n(b) individual\nCDR consumer for CDR data.\nNote:\nWhen CDR data and the other terms in the last column of the table\nappear in this notional version of Part IIIC, they have the same\nmeanings as in this Act."
    },
