    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56EY(5) Actions for damages",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The following are conferred with jurisdiction to hear and determine\nactions under subsection (1):\n\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court;\n\n(b) subject to the Constitution, the several courts of the\nTerritories.\nThis subsection does not enable an inferior court of a Territory to\ngrant a remedy of a kind that the court is unable to grant under the\nlaw of that Territory.\nNote:\nState courts and the Federal Court also have jurisdiction for these\nactions (see subsection 39(2) and paragraph 39B(1A)(c) of the\nJudiciary Act 1903).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The following are conferred with jurisdiction to hear and determine\nactions under subsection (1):\n\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court;\n\n(b) subject to the Constitution, the several courts of the\nTerritories.\nThis subsection does not enable an inferior court of a Territory to\ngrant a remedy of a kind that the court is unable to grant under the\nlaw of that Territory.\nNote:\nState courts and the Federal Court also have jurisdiction for these\nactions (see subsection 39(2) and paragraph 39B(1A)(c) of the\nJudiciary Act 1903).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ey"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b038aa3635ef872cf80721ba8da616204611cbc888c7817aa49fd5a81769e785",
      "skos:note": "Jurisdiction for actions under subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56EY(5) Actions for damages",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The following are conferred with jurisdiction to hear and determine\nactions under subsection (1):\n\n(a) the Federal Circuit Court;\n\n(b) subject to the Constitution, the several courts of the\nTerritories.\nThis subsection does not enable an inferior court of a Territory to\ngrant a remedy of a kind that the court is unable to grant under the\nlaw of that Territory.\nNote:\nState courts and the Federal Court also have jurisdiction for these\nactions (see subsection 39(2) and paragraph 39B(1A)(c) of the\nJudiciary Act 1903)."
    },
