    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FD Legal effect of data standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56fd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A contract is taken to be in force between:\n\n(a) a data holder of CDR data to which a binding data standard\napplies; and\n\n(b) each accredited person;\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nunder which each of those persons:\n\n(c) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard\napplies to the person; and\n\n(d) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the\nstandard to engage in.\nNote:\nThis means the data holder will be taken to have a separate contract\nwith each accredited person.\n\n(2) If there is a designated gateway for CDR data to which a binding\ndata standard applies, a contract is taken to be in force between:\n\n(a) a data holder of the CDR data; and\n\n(b) the designated gateway for the CDR data; and\n\n(c) each accredited person;\nunder which each of those persons:\n\n(d) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard\napplies to the person; and\n\n(e) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the\nstandard to engage in.\nNote:\nThis means the data holder will be taken to have a separate 3-party\ncontract with the designated gateway and each accredited person.\n\n(3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and\nthe consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the\nextent of the inconsistency.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A contract is taken to be in force between:\n\n(a) a data holder of CDR data to which a binding data standard\napplies; and\n\n(b) each accredited person;\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nunder which each of those persons:\n\n(c) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard\napplies to the person; and\n\n(d) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the\nstandard to engage in.\nNote:\nThis means the data holder will be taken to have a separate contract\nwith each accredited person.\n\n(2) If there is a designated gateway for CDR data to which a binding\ndata standard applies, a contract is taken to be in force between:\n\n(a) a data holder of the CDR data; and\n\n(b) the designated gateway for the CDR data; and\n\n(c) each accredited person;\nunder which each of those persons:\n\n(d) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard\napplies to the person; and\n\n(e) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the\nstandard to engage in.\nNote:\nThis means the data holder will be taken to have a separate 3-party\ncontract with the designated gateway and each accredited person.\n\n(3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and\nthe consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the\nextent of the inconsistency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee7d6bb9bd38b15c51ffb5b1bd930485a0e8bd11e4422611b98b51438f7b7ba9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56fd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FD Legal effect of data standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A contract is taken to be in force between:\n\n(a) a data holder of CDR data to which a binding data standard\napplies; and\n\n(b) each accredited person;\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\nunder which each of those persons:\n\n(c) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard\napplies to the person; and\n\n(d) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the\nstandard to engage in.\nNote:\nThis means the data holder will be taken to have a separate contract\nwith each accredited person.\n\n(2) If there is a designated gateway for CDR data to which a binding\ndata standard applies, a contract is taken to be in force between:\n\n(a) a data holder of the CDR data; and\n\n(b) the designated gateway for the CDR data; and\n\n(c) each accredited person;\nunder which each of those persons:\n\n(d) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard\napplies to the person; and\n\n(e) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the\nstandard to engage in.\nNote:\nThis means the data holder will be taken to have a separate 3-party\ncontract with the designated gateway and each accredited person.\n\n(3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and\nthe consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the\nextent of the inconsistency."
    },
