    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56FR Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56fr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the Data Standards\nChair:\n\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n\n(b) if the Data Standards Chair is unable to perform the duties of\nthe Data Standards Chair’s office because of physical or\nmental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the Data Standards\nChair if:\n\n(a) the Data Standards Chair:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with the Data Standards Chair’s creditors;\nor\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of the Data Standards Chair’s\nremuneration for the benefit of the Data Standards\nChair’s creditors; or\n\n(b) if the Data Standards Chair is appointed on a full-time\nbasis—the Data Standards Chair is absent, except on leave of\nabsence, for 14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any\n12-month period; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(c) the Data Standards Chair fails, without reasonable excuse, to\ncomply with section 29 of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 (which deals with\nthe duty to disclose interests) or rules made for the purposes\nof that section.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the Data Standards\nChair:\n\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n\n(b) if the Data Standards Chair is unable to perform the duties of\nthe Data Standards Chair’s office because of physical or\nmental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the Data Standards\nChair if:\n\n(a) the Data Standards Chair:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with the Data Standards Chair’s creditors;\nor\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of the Data Standards Chair’s\nremuneration for the benefit of the Data Standards\nChair’s creditors; or\n\n(b) if the Data Standards Chair is appointed on a full-time\nbasis—the Data Standards Chair is absent, except on leave of\nabsence, for 14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any\n12-month period; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(c) the Data Standards Chair fails, without reasonable excuse, to\ncomply with section 29 of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 (which deals with\nthe duty to disclose interests) or rules made for the purposes\nof that section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fr-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fr-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de9fa55d77ef891288a62d37dfd802f6a59e3f0146178f762ade910933ff469f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56fr",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56FR Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the Data Standards\nChair:\n\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n\n(b) if the Data Standards Chair is unable to perform the duties of\nthe Data Standards Chair’s office because of physical or\nmental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of the Data Standards\nChair if:\n\n(a) the Data Standards Chair:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with the Data Standards Chair’s creditors;\nor\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of the Data Standards Chair’s\nremuneration for the benefit of the Data Standards\nChair’s creditors; or\n\n(b) if the Data Standards Chair is appointed on a full-time\nbasis—the Data Standards Chair is absent, except on leave of\nabsence, for 14 consecutive days or for 28 days in any\n12-month period; or\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(c) the Data Standards Chair fails, without reasonable excuse, to\ncomply with section 29 of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 (which deals with\nthe duty to disclose interests) or rules made for the purposes\nof that section."
    },
    {
