    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56GD Exemptions by the Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56gd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a person, exempt\nthe person, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more\nclasses of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by\nthis section.\n\n(3) An exemption under subsection (2):\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a person, exempt\nthe person, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more\nclasses of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by\nthis section.\n\n(3) An exemption under subsection (2):\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1767b98a0b4ba4434a45e61a9513b113afbea9f566bd971b44420cdf72c4fd33"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56gd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GD Exemptions by the Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The Commission may, by written notice given to a person, exempt\nthe person, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more\nclasses of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by\nthis section.\n\n(3) An exemption under subsection (2):\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
