    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56GE Exemptions and modifications by regulations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ge"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The regulations may:\n\n(a) exempt a particular person, in relation to particular CDR data\nor one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified\nprovisions covered by this section; or\n\n(b) exempt a class of persons, in relation to particular CDR data\nor one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified\nprovisions covered by this section; or\n\n(c) declare that provisions covered by this section apply in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) a particular person in relation to particular CDR data or\none or more classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) a class of persons in relation to particular CDR data or\none or more classes of CDR data;\n\nas if specified provisions were omitted, modified or varied as\nspecified in the declaration.\n\n(3) An exemption under paragraph (2)(a) or (b), or a declaration under\nparagraph (2)(c):\n\n(a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The regulations may:\n\n(a) exempt a particular person, in relation to particular CDR data\nor one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified\nprovisions covered by this section; or\n\n(b) exempt a class of persons, in relation to particular CDR data\nor one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified\nprovisions covered by this section; or\n\n(c) declare that provisions covered by this section apply in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) a particular person in relation to particular CDR data or\none or more classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) a class of persons in relation to particular CDR data or\none or more classes of CDR data;\n\nas if specified provisions were omitted, modified or varied as\nspecified in the declaration.\n\n(3) An exemption under paragraph (2)(a) or (b), or a declaration under\nparagraph (2)(c):\n\n(a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92ed6a9017d9dd6c1e33087e4371c21378b8a09a9a8771367a9be9685ea5685e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56ge",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GE Exemptions and modifications by regulations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:\n\n(a) the following provisions:\n\n(i) the provisions of this Part;\n\n(ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of\nthe provisions of this Part;\n\n(iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and\n\n(b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data\nrules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in\nparagraph (a).\n\n(2) The regulations may:\n\n(a) exempt a particular person, in relation to particular CDR data\nor one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified\nprovisions covered by this section; or\n\n(b) exempt a class of persons, in relation to particular CDR data\nor one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified\nprovisions covered by this section; or\n\n(c) declare that provisions covered by this section apply in\nrelation to:\n\n(i) a particular person in relation to particular CDR data or\none or more classes of CDR data; or\n\n(ii) a class of persons in relation to particular CDR data or\none or more classes of CDR data;\n\nas if specified provisions were omitted, modified or varied as\nspecified in the declaration.\n\n(3) An exemption under paragraph (2)(a) or (b), or a declaration under\nparagraph (2)(c):\n\n(a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and\n\nConsumer data right  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 63, 2019\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019\n\n(b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions."
    },
