      "cml:integrityHash": "b5980e4f5cdd00e8a569c268d620ba0409aa5939467036445d89df4d137212a9",
      "skos:note": "Permits CDR entities to operate in specific contexts"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-56gf-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56GF(5) Constitutional basis",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The CDR provisions also have the effect they would have if their\noperation were expressly confined to CDR entities acting in the\ncourse of, or in relation to, any of the following:\n\n(a) trade or commerce between Australia and places outside\nAustralia;\n\n(b) trade or commerce among the States;\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
