    {
      "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Transitional—banking sector",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "Designating the banking sector\n(1)\nSubsections 56AD(2) and (3) and sections 56AE and 56AF of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010 do not apply in relation to an\ninstrument under subsection 56AC(2) of that Act that:\n\n(a) is to specify matters including:\n\n(i) one or more authorised deposit-taking institutions\n(within the meaning of the Banking Act 1959); or\n\n(ii) one or more classes of authorised deposit-taking\ninstitutions (within the meaning of the Banking Act\n1959);\n\nas holding one or more classes of information (or on whose\nbehalf such information is held); and\n\n(b) is to be made before the later of:\n\n(i) 1 July 2020; and\n\n(ii) the end of the 3-month period starting on the day this\nPart commences.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "skos:definition": "Designating the banking sector\n(1)\nSubsections 56AD(2) and (3) and sections 56AE and 56AF of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010 do not apply in relation to an\ninstrument under subsection 56AC(2) of that Act that:\n\n(a) is to specify matters including:\n\n(i) one or more authorised deposit-taking institutions\n(within the meaning of the Banking Act 1959); or\n\n(ii) one or more classes of authorised deposit-taking\ninstitutions (within the meaning of the Banking Act\n1959);\n\nas holding one or more classes of information (or on whose\nbehalf such information is held); and\n\n(b) is to be made before the later of:\n\n(i) 1 July 2020; and\n\n(ii) the end of the 3-month period starting on the day this\nPart commences.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2-logic-cogai-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-2-logic-shacl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e746c0e71bfafb345621e2ff7fa0b6aa335c4932e5b6274f3dea8b825db6e00b",
      "skos:note": "Exempts certain banking sector instruments from specific provisions of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019#sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Transitional—banking sector",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "Designating the banking sector\n(1)\nSubsections 56AD(2) and (3) and sections 56AE and 56AF of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010 do not apply in relation to an\ninstrument under subsection 56AC(2) of that Act that:\n\n(a) is to specify matters including:\n\n(i) one or more authorised deposit-taking institutions\n(within the meaning of the Banking Act 1959); or\n\n(ii) one or more classes of authorised deposit-taking\ninstitutions (within the meaning of the Banking Act\n1959);\n\nas holding one or more classes of information (or on whose\nbehalf such information is held); and\n\n(b) is to be made before the later of:\n\n(i) 1 July 2020; and\n\n(ii) the end of the 3-month period starting on the day this\nPart commences.\n\nSchedule 1  Consumer data right"
    },
    {
